IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wia-types`
IMPORT `wia-days`

-- Water Industry Act 1991 (UK) — GOAL 2: DISCONNECTION FOR NON-PAYMENT
-- (ss 61, 63(3), 63A, Schedule 4A).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1991-56.txt.
-- The customer asks: "Can my water be cut off for non-payment, and from
-- when; can a limiting device be used on my home?"

§ `Goal 2 — disconnection for non-payment`

-- s 61(1A): "The power conferred by subsection (1) above is not exercisable
-- in relation to any premises specified in Schedule 4A".
@ref s 61(1A), Sch 4A
@export Are my premises protected from disconnection for non-payment by Schedule 4A to the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? Yes for a dwelling, house in multiple occupation or accommodation for the elderly that is someone's only or principal home, and for the other premises Schedule 4A lists (hospitals, surgeries, care homes, schools, prisons, emergency services and others). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of premises`  @desc The kind of premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` k IF
    NOT (k EQUALS `premises not listed in Schedule 4A`)

-- s 61(1ZA)(b): the occupier "has failed to do so before the end of the
-- period of seven days beginning with the day after he is served with
-- notice". Payment by the service day + 7 is in time; the power arises on the
-- service day + 8. A later payment does not end it (F4).
@ref s 61(1ZA)
GIVEN c IS A `Non-payment case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay for` c MEANS `the day` 7 `days after` (c's `payment notice served on`)

-- s 61(2)-(3): a counter-notice "within the period of seven days" (which
-- begins with the day after service, so a counter-notice on the day of
-- service is not within it: changed after the independent pass) disputing
-- liability
-- bars the power unless a judgment for the charges is enforceable or a
-- settlement agreement made since is in breach.
@ref s 61(2)-(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Non-payment case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a counter-notice bars the power for` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `counter-notice served on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST k  THEN
            k GREATER THAN c's `payment notice served on`
        AND k AT MOST `the last day to pay for` c
        AND NOT (c's `a judgment for the charges is enforceable` OR c's `a settlement agreement is in breach`)

@ref s 61(1), (1ZA), (1A), (2)-(3)
@export From what day may the water undertaker cut off my supply for non-payment under s 61 of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? Not at all for premises in Schedule 4A; otherwise, if I am liable for the charges and did not pay within the seven days beginning with the day after I was served with notice, from the eighth day after service — unless I served a counter-notice within those seven days disputing liability and no judgment is enforceable and no settlement is in breach. NOTHING where there is no power. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Non-payment case`  @desc The premises, my liability, the notice and any payment or counter-notice
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest day my water can be cut off for` c MEANS
    IF     `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` (c's `the premises`)
        OR NOT (c's `I am liable for the charges`)
        OR paidInTime
        OR `a counter-notice bars the power for` c
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the day` 1 `days after` (`the last day to pay for` c))
    WHERE
        paidInTime MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `paid on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST p  THEN p AT MOST `the last day to pay for` c

@ref s 61(1)
@export May the water undertaker cut off my supply for non-payment on the day it did (or proposes to), under s 61 of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Non-payment case`  @desc The non-payment facts and the day of the cut-off
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my water may be cut off on the day for` c IF
    CONSIDER `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST e  THEN c's `cut off on` AT LEAST e

-- s 63(3)(a): the undertaker is guilty of an offence if it cuts off a supply
-- where it has no power to do so (here, under s 61).
@ref s 63(3)(a)
@export Would cutting off my supply on that day for non-payment be an offence by the water undertaker under s 63(3)(a) of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? Yes if s 61 gives it no power to do so that day. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Non-payment case`  @desc The non-payment facts and the day of the cut-off
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cutting off would be an offence for` c IF
    NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` c)

-- s 63A(1): using a limiting device on Schedule 4A premises to enforce
-- payment is an offence.
@ref s 63A(1)
@export Would fitting a limiting device to enforce payment be an offence under s 63A of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? Yes for premises listed in Schedule 4A. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of premises`  @desc The kind of premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limiting device would be an offence for` k IF
    `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` k
